/-! # VII-05 (F2c2): right-side vanishing ⇒ finite coefficient conditions

1. **One-sided zero lemma.** If `g` is `C^∞` at `0` and `g = 0` on `(0, ε)`, then every
   `iteratedDeriv k g 0 = 0`: first `iteratedDeriv k g = 0` on the open set `(0, ε)`
   (`Set.EqOn.iteratedDeriv_of_isOpen`), then the value at `0` is the limit along `𝓝[>] 0`
   of a function continuous at `0` (`tendsto_nhds_unique`). Only right-side equality is used;
   nothing is assumed on `(-ε, 0)`, and a single value `g(0) = 0` is never used to kill
   derivatives (controls in `SmoothBranchControls.lean`).
2. **Actual residuals match the actual residual polynomials below degree five.** Through the
   VII-04 weighted bodies (`pcE_eq_pcW`, `polyPC_eq`) and the subring `matchRing`, the real
   `realPC h Q J F b A` matches `polyPC h Q J (jet4 F) (jet4 b) (jet4 A)` (same for `PM`, `PA`).
3. **Γ through its fourth-order core.** `realCore` is the real-function instance of the
   `gammaCore` body (`coreE`); on any point where `F` and `A'` are differentiable,
   `realGamma = x⁴ · realCore` (genuine `HasDerivAt` for `δ(δA)` and `δ(x² F)`). Division by
   `x⁴` happens only for `x > 0`.

Consequences: right-side vanishing of `realPM realPA realPC` gives the eight VII-04
`SelectedRows` for `jet4 F, jet4 b, jet4 A`; right-side vanishing of `realGamma` gives
`gammaGen` coefficients 6, 7, 8 zero. The two sources are kept separate. -/

